  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "City traffic",
  "description": "The cones are the town limits and the ball is your car. Everyone has a stick and a ball and skates around town without crashing and without leaving it. The coach calls out traffic signals: “Green” – full speed, “Red” – stop and keep the ball still at the blade, “Reverse” – pull the ball back with the stick, “Roundabout” – turn and skate the other way, “Speed bump” – bend your knees as deep as you can and keep skating. Make up your own signals with the children.\n\nAfter a while a car thief comes in, with a stick but no ball. The thief tries to steal a car, and whoever loses their ball becomes the new thief. The thief may only play the ball, never hit sticks or legs. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up so you can see where the ice is free."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the ball close to the blade so you have time to stop and turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Change direction and speed with your edges when someone comes close."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Stick low and blade on the ice – nobody lifts their stick or hits someone else’s."
    }
  ],
